{"ts": "2026-10-16T09:47:28.853062Z", "run_id": "r-20261016T0920Z-ec4a", "unit": "openspec:add-telemetry-runtime", "seq": 83, "type": "task.done", "task": "2.1", "base": "b791bfedde72a4f579a108526430047c74352514", "parents": [], "notes": "Task 2.1 touches only OTelSettings (config.py); telemetry.py got two minimal compatibility lines because changing enabled from bool to the string mode would otherwise break already-passing frozen tests: (1) init_telemetry now treats only the literal 'true' as on, so 'false' and 'auto' stay off exactly as the old bool default did until task 3 builds the enablement logic; (2) Resource.create falls back to 'mintmory' when service_name is None (the old default), keeping the api metric-exporter test's resource valid. Annotation note: the task text says enabled: Literal[...]; I declared it Literal['auto','true','false'] | bool because the frozen packages/api/tests/test_health_and_otel.py still calls OTelSettings(enabled=True) and the harness runs mypy strict over tests. Runtime still normalises bools to 'true'/'false', so the field always holds the string. Accepted findings: F-1619b9 (one WARNING per bad shared variable; protocol checked once) and F-0ad188 (_Scrubbing keeps _inner) target the 'Bad standard values fall back' and scrubber/7.1 scenarios, which belong to tasks 3/4/4b, not 2.1; nothing in 2.1 needs them. F-fea82d, F-5d64eb and F-f4dc92 are informational gaps for later tasks; not applicable here. No test, fixture or conftest was edited. Gate: 1598 passed, 114 skipped; ruff check/format and mypy packages all clean.", "suppressions": []}
